      "message": "This CL duplicates the logic here: https://review.coreboot.org/c/coreboot/+/68471\n\nThat means any tuning must occur in both repos, which we wanted to avoid with the original description here: b/232946420#comment98\n\n\u003e To make that work though, the EC will need to be updated to send EC_HOST_EVENT_THERMAL_THRESHOLD at the appropriate time. One idea that rrangle@ had was for the EC to send it whenever the sensor value changes by +/-1deg C. This way the EC doesn\u0027t need to know any of the 40/45/50/55deg C threshold values defined in the flow chart. Instead, that logic can all be in a single place: dptc.asl.\n\nInstead, to remove the duplication the earlier CL should be updated to implement that logic:\n4054309: common: body_detection: notify host to switch thermal table | https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/4054309",
